== Multiplications per Corollary 2 point addition (paper's own constraint list)
   modular multiplications per addition >= 23; integer multiplications >= 46
   b=131: >= 700580 edges per point addition from multiplications alone (= 5348 edges per bit); hash slot adds 2 x 15234 edges
   b=256: >= 780068 edges per point addition from multiplications alone (= 3047 edges per bit); hash slot adds 2 x 30326 edges
   ECCp-131 m=2 implementation: 1,564,506 edges / (2*131) = 5971 edges per slot-bit; receipt lists 34 x 131-bit + 4 x 132-bit integer products.
   Lemma 7 upper bound for 38 products at d<=132: 5559400 edges (>= 1,564,506: consistent).

== D.4 admission thresholds (OpenAI preprint, quantitative-contraction.tex eqs. parameters/bounds)
   u_0 = floor(lambda/2^17) >= 1            <=> lambda >= 2^17   (Bochum 'size 2^(2^17)')
   u_0 >= lambda^(4/5) at depth 0           <=> lambda >= 2^85   (clustering note item 1)
   u_d >= lambda^(4/5) at the deepest active call d ~ log2(lambda)/6  <=> lambda >= 2^510 (C=1)
   check: lambda=2^85: u0=295147905179352825856, lambda^0.8=295147905179352825856: equal -> boundary correct
   check: lambda=2^510: d_max=85, u_d=2^408, lambda^0.8=2^408 -> equal: boundary correct
   L09 margin formula: 0.2*log2(lambda) - 17 at lambda=10.21 -> -16.33 ; at lambda=21.96 -> -16.11 (table2.json: -16.33 .. -16.11)
   ECCp-131 graph: s=1,564,506 -> lambda=21, u_0=0, exact leaf 2^s; the receipt agrees (root_u 0).

