== Exponent comparison (bits), taking D.1 as the formula c*s/sqrt(log2 s) with c=1 at every size
   s = a*m*b edges; a=1 is the impossible floor (interface only), a=2600 is the paper's own gadget floor,
   a=6000 is the implementation at b=131.  rho = b/2.  Naive enumeration per attempt = (m-1)b/m.
   b=128 a=    1: best m=3: solver/attempt 1.311e+02 bits, calls 52.8, lin.alg 146.8; total 1.839e+02 bits vs rho 64, enumeration/attempt 85.3
   b=128 a= 2600: best m=2: solver/attempt 1.513e+05 bits, calls 73.0, lin.alg 209.0; total 1.514e+05 bits vs rho 64, enumeration/attempt 64.0
